## 2. What was attempted: batch 3 (D7.1, /+5V_ESP, one 100 nF)

Batch 3 was chosen because it is a single part, so it could be finished rather than half-done. The plan was
C52, 100 nF, cloned from C41 (same `MoriShield_Carrier:C_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.18x1.45mm_HandSolder`
footprint already on the board), symbol at a grid point, label `+5V_ESP` on pin 1 (net `/+5V_ESP`), GND power
symbol on pin 2; board at (215.60, 97.50) rot 90, pad 1 to D7.1 at (215.60, 103.00) - 4.46 mm along the
copper - and its own GND via at (213.50, 96.46), not shared with anything.

**Attempt 1 failed, four ways:**
- the board footprint's `at` line did not match my regex, so C52 landed on top of C41 (`courtyards_overlap`,
  two `silk_overlap`, `shorting_items` with C41's pad 1);
- pad 1 kept C41's `+5V` net instead of `/+5V_ESP` (`net_conflict`);
- the schematic symbol x = 455 is off the 1.27 mm grid (two `endpoint_off_grid` in ERC).

**Attempt 2 fixed two of the three** - pad 1 became `/+5V_ESP` (parity back to 0) and the symbol moved to
454.66, on grid - **but the `at` regex missed again**: KiCad writes a footprint's `at` without the rotation
field when the rotation is 0, so `\(at [-\d.]+ [-\d.]+ [-\d.]+\)` matched a property `at` line instead and
C52 stayed at C41's position. Result: 9 violations, 1 unconnected, and a `shorting_items` between C41.1 and
C52.1.

Per the batch rule, the snapshot `pcb\_snap\T59_5VESP_20261104_090758` was restored.

