## 4. Root cause, and the fix for the next run

**Cloning a board footprint by regex on `(at ...)` is unsafe.** Two traps, both hit here: KiCad omits the
rotation field when it is 0, and `(at ...)` also appears in every property. The footprint's own placement
node must be taken from the s-expression parser as the `at` child of the footprint node, not found by text
pattern. With that one change the batch-3 edit should apply first time; the rest of it (pad nets, label,
GND symbol, track, via) already produced parity 0 in attempt 2.

